WEBVTT

00:00:07.400 --> 00:00:09.190
<i>Who the hell are you?!</i>

00:00:10.680 --> 00:00:14.960
<i>I'm known as Murakami 
Zanzo, the Executioner.</i>

00:00:15.830 --> 00:00:18.080
<i>I shall send you to hell.</i>

00:00:18.450 --> 00:00:19.830
<i>Hosokawa-sama!</i>

00:00:23.020 --> 00:00:24.150
<i>Kill him!</i>

00:00:41.060 --> 00:00:45.530
<b>Silver Fox</b>

00:02:01.990 --> 00:02:05.880
<b>Makoto's Future</b>

00:02:04.820 --> 00:02:08.800
Yes, Okawa Shigeto is so cool!

00:02:12.910 --> 00:02:14.820
Did you enjoy it, Gin?

00:02:15.060 --> 00:02:17.280
Yeah, the same thing 
happens every episode.

00:02:18.470 --> 00:02:19.590
Dad.

00:02:19.590 --> 00:02:20.140
Hmm?

00:02:20.140 --> 00:02:22.010
Gin says the same thing 
happens every episode.

00:02:22.310 --> 00:02:25.060
The same thing happens, 
but it's still good.

00:02:26.580 --> 00:02:27.770
I know.

00:02:28.290 --> 00:02:30.790
I borrowed the movie, 
so we can watch that.

00:02:30.790 --> 00:02:33.460
Gintaro-sama should enjoy this.

00:02:33.670 --> 00:02:34.890
Huh?!

00:02:34.890 --> 00:02:36.920
Don't you need to prepare for 
the cleansing ceremony, Dad?

00:02:37.140 --> 00:02:39.670
I've finished everything 
that I can do today.

00:02:39.670 --> 00:02:43.760
No! You have to go pick 
up the thatch tomorrow!

00:02:43.760 --> 00:02:45.010
Go to bed!

00:02:45.010 --> 00:02:47.730
You've grown hard.

00:02:47.730 --> 00:02:51.330
When you were little, 
you said that you wanted to be

00:02:51.330 --> 00:02:53.190
my bride when you grew up.

00:02:53.190 --> 00:02:54.500
When did I say that?

00:02:55.860 --> 00:02:56.880
This can't be...

00:02:57.600 --> 00:03:00.290
Hey, don't make Tatsuo cry.

00:03:00.290 --> 00:03:01.360
It's annoying.

00:03:03.360 --> 00:03:05.580
S-Sorry, Dad...

00:03:06.040 --> 00:03:09.870
Well, Zanzo's over, 
so I should get going.

00:03:11.350 --> 00:03:15.460
Gin, you said it's the same thing 
every time, but you still like it.

00:03:17.030 --> 00:03:19.230
A bride, huh...

00:03:20.240 --> 00:03:23.800
I'm okay with any job that 
lets me touch animals.

00:03:24.330 --> 00:03:25.550
I'm going to college.

00:03:25.810 --> 00:03:28.970
I'm thinking about becoming 
a chef or nutritionist.

00:03:29.340 --> 00:03:31.120
I need to worry about what

00:03:31.120 --> 00:03:33.020
I'm doing after I graduate 
from high school first.

00:03:33.520 --> 00:03:35.720
I was talking about it with 
my classmates the other day,

00:03:35.720 --> 00:03:38.360
and I was surprised that 
they've all given it thought.

00:03:39.530 --> 00:03:41.920
Is there something you want to do?

00:03:41.920 --> 00:03:42.800
Huh?

00:03:42.800 --> 00:03:46.830
I got to choose what 
to do with my life.

00:03:48.800 --> 00:03:51.820
Your mother had a lot 
of things she still wanted to do...

00:03:52.510 --> 00:03:55.000
but she had no choice 
but to take over this shrine.

00:03:55.950 --> 00:03:59.200
She said that she wanted 
you to have a choice.

00:04:00.370 --> 00:04:03.130
So I think you should do what you want,

00:04:03.510 --> 00:04:06.680
and if you fall in love, 
you can get married.

00:04:07.210 --> 00:04:11.020
I'll support you, 
no matter what you decide.

00:04:22.860 --> 00:04:25.110
Gin, you're still here?

00:04:25.110 --> 00:04:27.320
Hey, turn the lights off.

00:04:27.940 --> 00:04:29.380
You were awake anyway.

00:04:31.600 --> 00:04:34.020
What? You're creeping me out.

00:04:34.890 --> 00:04:35.840
Hey, Gin...

00:04:36.370 --> 00:04:41.250
I wanted to become a shrine 
maiden like Mom was.

00:04:41.990 --> 00:04:45.470
But I can barely remember 
what she was like...

00:04:46.100 --> 00:04:49.670
So I think I just wanted to 
know what my mom was like.

00:04:50.080 --> 00:04:52.390
Oh, you want to talk about your future.

00:04:52.390 --> 00:04:56.010
Humans spend a lot of time 
on that topic these days.

00:04:56.010 --> 00:04:58.060
If you want to know 
about Yuko, ask Tatsuo.

00:04:58.510 --> 00:05:01.820
Dad has a biased view.

00:05:02.480 --> 00:05:04.590
I was talking to him earlier.

00:05:05.740 --> 00:05:08.070
He told me to do what I want to do.

00:05:08.070 --> 00:05:09.780
That's great, then.

00:05:10.530 --> 00:05:13.870
Say, did Mom want to 
become a shrine maiden?

00:05:14.150 --> 00:05:16.350
Did she want to become one?

00:05:16.350 --> 00:05:19.850
It felt like that was the 
only choice she had.

00:05:20.370 --> 00:05:23.590
She had health problems and 
couldn't go outside too much.

00:05:24.100 --> 00:05:28.550
Does that mean she never 
got to realize her dreams?

00:05:28.760 --> 00:05:30.500
I wouldn't say that.

00:05:31.040 --> 00:05:34.270
She married Tatsuo despite the 
objections from everyone around.

00:05:34.540 --> 00:05:36.270
Wait, what?

00:05:36.270 --> 00:05:38.450
People didn't want Mom 
and Dad to get married?

00:05:38.880 --> 00:05:40.110
Pretty much.

00:05:40.540 --> 00:05:42.360
I wanted to become a

00:05:42.360 --> 00:05:44.390
shrine maiden because 
that was what Mom was.

00:05:44.780 --> 00:05:47.260
I wanted to know what Mom used to do.

00:05:48.310 --> 00:05:50.630
I still think shrine maidens are

00:05:50.630 --> 00:05:54.090
special and important 
servants of the gods.

00:06:03.200 --> 00:06:05.550
But it's not the same now...

00:06:05.550 --> 00:06:06.720
I didn't want to become 
a shrine maiden.

00:06:08.360 --> 00:06:09.930
I just wanted

00:06:11.100 --> 00:06:13.310
to be like Mom...

00:06:17.700 --> 00:06:20.260
I'm getting sick of 
thinking about this.

00:06:21.140 --> 00:06:23.820
I wish you could divine 
my future for me.

00:06:24.060 --> 00:06:25.670
Hey, don't act like a spoiled brat.

00:06:26.300 --> 00:06:27.320
You're so mean.

00:06:27.820 --> 00:06:30.090
Well, I wouldn't be 
able to do it, anyway.

00:06:30.540 --> 00:06:31.530
Really?

00:06:31.960 --> 00:06:37.200
For some reason, I can't see the 
future of someone with the Sight.

00:06:37.200 --> 00:06:39.470
Well, I don't care to find 
out when someone I know

00:06:39.470 --> 00:06:41.540
is going to die, so I'm not interested.

00:06:42.310 --> 00:06:45.160
It's not very fun when you 
know everything beforehand.

00:06:45.160 --> 00:06:46.320
Oh...

00:06:47.720 --> 00:06:48.970
That reminds me.

00:06:49.550 --> 00:06:53.170
Did I really say that I 
wanted to be Dad's bride?

00:06:53.170 --> 00:06:54.030
Yeah.

00:06:54.920 --> 00:06:56.200
That's cute.

00:06:56.200 --> 00:06:57.490
I probably told you the same thing.

00:06:57.490 --> 00:06:58.980
Don't think so.

00:06:59.390 --> 00:07:00.380
Really?

00:07:00.970 --> 00:07:04.290
Still, I don't know what to do...

00:07:04.290 --> 00:07:06.330
Well, it's your future.

00:07:06.330 --> 00:07:08.440
So do what you want.

00:07:08.670 --> 00:07:10.720
Come on, Gin!

00:07:10.720 --> 00:07:12.880
Stop talking and go to bed.

00:07:12.880 --> 00:07:14.410
Don't you have a busy day tomorrow?

00:07:17.240 --> 00:07:19.810
Jeez! Stupid Gintaro!

00:07:25.350 --> 00:07:26.840
Turn off the lights.

00:07:43.940 --> 00:07:49.900
<i>The number you have dialed is 
not available at the moment.</i>

00:07:50.070 --> 00:07:52.190
Man, he's not answering his phone!

00:07:53.000 --> 00:07:55.590
I haven't heard anything since 
he said he was running late!

00:07:55.590 --> 00:07:57.660
Where'd he go?!

00:07:57.830 --> 00:08:00.620
Keep it down. And calm down.

00:08:01.020 --> 00:08:03.290
But it's already noon!

00:08:03.290 --> 00:08:05.690
He said he'd be back by ten!

00:08:07.150 --> 00:08:09.920
Gin, can you divine where Dad is?

00:08:09.920 --> 00:08:11.050
Requires too much effort.

00:08:11.570 --> 00:08:12.240
What?!

00:08:12.680 --> 00:08:13.710
More importantly,

00:08:13.710 --> 00:08:16.740
we need to finish cleaning 
up before your dad returns.

00:08:17.450 --> 00:08:20.080
Look. There are still weeds.

00:08:20.540 --> 00:08:22.450
You're not gonna accomplish 
anything by throwing a fit.

00:08:22.450 --> 00:08:24.180
He'll be back soon enough.

00:08:25.320 --> 00:08:27.310
Stop bothering Gintaro-sama.

00:08:27.760 --> 00:08:29.340
S-Sorry...

00:08:29.340 --> 00:08:33.150
There's one day left and you still 
haven't finished the wreath?

00:08:33.400 --> 00:08:36.240
Well, we usually take it slow.

00:08:38.810 --> 00:08:40.230
"Usually"...

00:08:40.230 --> 00:08:42.500
Satoru, are you okay?

00:08:44.110 --> 00:08:46.230
Saeki! Kamio!

00:08:47.450 --> 00:08:49.280
Yumi-chan! Funabashi-san!

00:08:50.250 --> 00:08:51.440
Don't you have school?

00:08:51.440 --> 00:08:53.110
We skipped out!

00:08:53.110 --> 00:08:56.510
Fifth period is study hour 
and sixth period is music.

00:08:56.510 --> 00:08:57.800
Funabashi-san also skipped?

00:08:58.750 --> 00:09:01.070
She's turning into a bad girl!

00:09:01.070 --> 00:09:02.500
And her reason for coming is naughty.

00:09:02.500 --> 00:09:03.770
Um, I...

00:09:04.040 --> 00:09:07.530
Right, everybody's talking 
because both of you

00:09:07.530 --> 00:09:09.010
are absent from school!

00:09:09.010 --> 00:09:09.750
What?!

00:09:09.750 --> 00:09:10.620
Just kidding!

00:09:11.450 --> 00:09:12.740
They're so loud.

00:09:13.210 --> 00:09:15.000
So what's this?

00:09:15.000 --> 00:09:16.030
Oh, this is...

00:09:16.030 --> 00:09:17.230
Makoto-chan!

00:09:18.060 --> 00:09:20.410
We're almost finished. 
Where's the Chief Priest?

00:09:22.320 --> 00:09:23.970
I'm so sorry!

00:09:23.970 --> 00:09:26.200
My dad isn't answering his phone!

00:09:26.520 --> 00:09:29.350
Jeez, where'd he go?!

00:09:29.350 --> 00:09:31.210
Now, calm down.

00:09:31.210 --> 00:09:32.380
What's going on?

00:09:32.810 --> 00:09:35.490
My dad went with his friend 
from another shrine

00:09:35.490 --> 00:09:37.570
to pick up thatch, 
but they aren't back yet!

00:09:37.870 --> 00:09:39.580
Is the thatch for the wreath?

00:09:39.580 --> 00:09:40.760
Yes!

00:09:40.760 --> 00:09:41.720
Wreath?

00:09:41.720 --> 00:09:44.070
We wrap the grass around 
this ring to make a wreath.

00:09:44.070 --> 00:09:46.660
It's absolutely needed 
for tomorrow's ceremony!

00:09:46.660 --> 00:09:48.520
Oh, this ring?

00:09:48.520 --> 00:09:50.630
Anyway, please take a break.

00:09:50.630 --> 00:09:51.730
I'll get you something to drink.

00:09:51.730 --> 00:09:53.180
Oh, thanks.

00:09:55.740 --> 00:09:57.400
Do we have enough tea?

00:09:59.090 --> 00:10:01.890
Saeki! The boss guy 
wants to talk to you!

00:10:01.890 --> 00:10:03.220
Oh, okay!

00:10:03.470 --> 00:10:05.310
Funabashi-san, can you wait one moment.

00:10:05.310 --> 00:10:05.950
Yes.

00:10:16.380 --> 00:10:18.260
Man, that sucked.

00:10:18.500 --> 00:10:21.220
The highway was jammed 
because of an accident.

00:10:21.660 --> 00:10:24.780
Oh, sorry. I thought you were 
the girl who lives here.

00:10:26.160 --> 00:10:26.930
Hello.

00:10:27.520 --> 00:10:28.760
Hello...

00:10:29.430 --> 00:10:30.960
Hey, Tatsuo!

00:10:30.960 --> 00:10:33.290
There's a really pretty 
girl in your kitchen!

00:10:33.290 --> 00:10:35.220
How'd you get her inside your house?

00:10:35.220 --> 00:10:36.000
What?

00:10:36.570 --> 00:10:37.860
Oh.

00:10:38.570 --> 00:10:40.320
She's Makoto's friend.

00:10:40.540 --> 00:10:42.070
Oh, really?

00:10:42.070 --> 00:10:44.100
Welcome, Funabashi-san.

00:10:44.100 --> 00:10:45.460
Thank you for inviting us.

00:10:49.460 --> 00:10:50.960
Mako-chan!

00:10:51.180 --> 00:10:53.180
Oh, Uncle Yoshitomo!

00:10:53.180 --> 00:10:55.920
What? Who's that handsome guy?!

00:10:56.240 --> 00:10:58.880
Jeez, stupid! You're late!

00:10:59.120 --> 00:11:01.120
Sorry, haven't seen you in a while.

00:11:01.120 --> 00:11:02.480
Everyone, please have 
something to drink.

00:11:02.480 --> 00:11:07.060
You'll filled out a bit 
since I last saw you.

00:11:07.340 --> 00:11:09.240
What?! That's a priest?!

00:11:09.520 --> 00:11:12.430
I thought you weren't 
interested in older men.

00:11:12.430 --> 00:11:13.900
Handsome ones are an exception!

00:11:14.210 --> 00:11:15.520
Don't worry.

00:11:15.520 --> 00:11:18.480
I'll take responsibility by 
making you my bride.

00:11:19.090 --> 00:11:20.640
That's great, Makoto.

00:11:20.640 --> 00:11:22.340
No way!

00:11:22.340 --> 00:11:25.190
Hey, you shouldn't be laughing!

00:11:25.190 --> 00:11:28.210
Mako-chan's like a daughter to me.

00:11:28.210 --> 00:11:31.460
I'm always worrying about her 
ending up with some bad apple.

00:11:33.000 --> 00:11:35.130
Looks like I'm too late...

00:11:35.130 --> 00:11:37.420
Oh, this is Satoru-kun.

00:11:37.740 --> 00:11:40.000
Oh, you're the boy from Kamio shrine.

00:11:40.000 --> 00:11:40.740
Yes...

00:11:41.880 --> 00:11:44.670
Right, I hear that you also...

00:11:49.030 --> 00:11:52.700
Jeez! Why didn't you 
answer your phone, Dad?!

00:11:52.700 --> 00:11:53.350
Huh?

00:11:54.210 --> 00:11:55.970
Oh, it's out of power.

00:11:55.970 --> 00:11:56.990
Jeez!

00:11:56.990 --> 00:11:59.650
Anyway, Saeki... 
How about some introductions?

00:12:00.000 --> 00:12:03.460
Oh, right. This is my dad's friend.

00:12:03.460 --> 00:12:05.240
Oh, I'm Takami Yoshitomo.

00:12:05.520 --> 00:12:07.380
Uh, Funabashi-san?

00:12:07.380 --> 00:12:08.580
Sorry about what happened earlier.

00:12:08.850 --> 00:12:12.040
I was thinking that Tatsuo had 
found himself a young lover.

00:12:12.180 --> 00:12:13.730
Don't be silly.

00:12:15.450 --> 00:12:17.500
I'm Ikegami Yumi!

00:12:17.500 --> 00:12:19.360
So, are you really a priest?

00:12:19.360 --> 00:12:22.220
Oh, I'm actually retired,

00:12:22.220 --> 00:12:25.180
but I help out when needed.

00:12:25.510 --> 00:12:26.850
Which is every time there's a ceremony.

00:12:26.850 --> 00:12:28.810
We appreciate the help.

00:12:29.070 --> 00:12:31.250
<i>His lover...</i>

00:12:32.180 --> 00:12:33.070
<i>Stop it!</i>

00:12:33.070 --> 00:12:34.770
<i>He's my friend's father!</i>

00:12:34.770 --> 00:12:36.290
<i>I'm sorry, Saeki-san!</i>

00:12:37.460 --> 00:12:39.580
So what do you do when 
you aren't a priest?

00:12:39.580 --> 00:12:41.240
I own a bar.

00:12:42.220 --> 00:12:46.210
People like the idea of a 
bar run by a former priest.

00:12:42.220 --> 00:12:47.950
Gintaro

00:12:46.210 --> 00:12:47.950
We even offer purifications.

00:12:48.190 --> 00:12:49.760
That sounds interesting!

00:12:49.760 --> 00:12:51.670
That doesn't seem right.

00:12:49.760 --> 00:12:51.670
There are more strangers around.

00:12:51.670 --> 00:12:53.040
It's just for show.

00:12:51.670 --> 00:12:53.040
That's what happens when 
there's a festival.

00:12:53.040 --> 00:12:57.950
But it's still quieter 
than our old shrine.

00:12:57.950 --> 00:13:02.070
Well, festivals are important, 
so we should support them.

00:13:02.400 --> 00:13:04.760
But is that guy really a priest?

00:13:04.760 --> 00:13:06.270
You mean Yoshitomo?

00:13:06.270 --> 00:13:07.470
You know him?

00:13:07.620 --> 00:13:09.420
He comes every year.

00:13:09.420 --> 00:13:11.430
Etsuko should be here soon.

00:13:11.430 --> 00:13:12.530
Etsuko?

00:13:12.530 --> 00:13:13.430
And there she is.

00:13:21.980 --> 00:13:27.860
<b>Silver Fox</b>

00:13:22.680 --> 00:13:23.500
Honestly...

00:13:25.670 --> 00:13:30.330
Hey! If you park the van there, 
nobody else can get in!

00:13:30.960 --> 00:13:31.660
Oh?

00:13:32.310 --> 00:13:34.010
Everyone's here.

00:13:34.010 --> 00:13:35.600
Oh. Sorry, Sis.

00:13:35.600 --> 00:13:36.870
I'll unload the thatch now.

00:13:37.360 --> 00:13:38.620
It's his...

00:13:38.620 --> 00:13:39.590
Sister?

00:13:39.890 --> 00:13:41.900
Oh, Takami-kun's also here.

00:13:41.900 --> 00:13:44.030
Hello, I'm back again.

00:13:44.030 --> 00:13:47.430
You aren't up to any rogue 
priest antics, are you?

00:13:47.430 --> 00:13:49.600
Such as performing 
purifications at your bar?

00:13:50.900 --> 00:13:53.060
Th-That's crazy talk.

00:13:53.640 --> 00:13:55.750
Tatsuo, I brought some sake.

00:13:55.750 --> 00:13:57.810
We have a good batch this year.

00:13:57.970 --> 00:13:59.340
Really?

00:13:59.340 --> 00:14:01.320
Mom and Dad said they'll 
be here tomorrow.

00:14:01.320 --> 00:14:04.260
Oh, I'm sure they must be busy.

00:14:04.260 --> 00:14:05.990
Thank your husband for me.

00:14:07.220 --> 00:14:09.490
Oh, are you Satoru-kun?

00:14:09.830 --> 00:14:11.410
It's nice to meet you.

00:14:12.030 --> 00:14:13.990
Oh, Aunt Etsuko. Let me introduce you.

00:14:13.990 --> 00:14:14.910
These are my friends.

00:14:17.330 --> 00:14:20.130
Have we met before?

00:14:20.390 --> 00:14:21.210
Huh?

00:14:21.590 --> 00:14:23.380
Hiwako-sama!

00:14:25.610 --> 00:14:27.850
What's wrong, Yoshizumi-san?

00:14:27.850 --> 00:14:30.220
You left your cell phone in the car.

00:14:30.220 --> 00:14:31.780
Oh, no!

00:14:31.780 --> 00:14:32.510
Oh?

00:14:32.990 --> 00:14:33.930
Huh?

00:14:34.540 --> 00:14:36.930
Aren't you Funabashi-sensei's 
assistant?

00:14:36.930 --> 00:14:38.850
Mrs. Toyokura?

00:14:39.170 --> 00:14:40.620
H-Hello!

00:14:40.620 --> 00:14:42.330
Allow me to thank you for 
your continued support.

00:14:42.720 --> 00:14:44.430
What brings you here today?

00:14:44.430 --> 00:14:46.940
Oh, I'm here as an escort 
for Hiwako-sama.

00:14:47.400 --> 00:14:49.070
Hiwako-sama?

00:14:49.660 --> 00:14:50.530
What?!

00:14:50.530 --> 00:14:52.410
Funabashi-sensei's daughter?!

00:14:52.410 --> 00:14:54.620
Toyokura? What?

00:14:54.910 --> 00:14:56.260
Huh? What's going on?

00:14:56.560 --> 00:15:00.260
Oh, my dad's last name 
used to be Toyokura.

00:15:00.260 --> 00:15:01.740
Toyokura?

00:15:01.740 --> 00:15:04.170
As in Toyokura Brewery?

00:15:04.170 --> 00:15:04.630
Yep.

00:15:05.090 --> 00:15:08.500
What?!

00:15:06.500 --> 00:15:07.710
Toyokura Brewery

00:15:10.130 --> 00:15:14.850
<b>Toyokura</b>

00:15:10.130 --> 00:15:14.850
<b>Toyokura 
Brewery</b>

00:15:10.350 --> 00:15:13.490
Toyokura Brewery is a local specialty!

00:15:13.490 --> 00:15:14.850
Even I've heard of it!

00:15:15.200 --> 00:15:16.870
Yeah, this is a shock...

00:15:16.870 --> 00:15:19.230
You also come from a rich family...

00:15:19.230 --> 00:15:21.680
No, no. We're not rich at all.

00:15:21.680 --> 00:15:24.400
Please, we're not rich or anything.

00:15:24.400 --> 00:15:26.070
And business has been poor lately.

00:15:26.180 --> 00:15:28.260
Wait...

00:15:28.870 --> 00:15:30.820
The priest is Toyokura-sama's son?

00:15:31.100 --> 00:15:32.920
That's right.

00:15:32.920 --> 00:15:35.400
That boy was supposed to 
inherit the business,

00:15:35.400 --> 00:15:37.530
but he fell in love with 
the shrine maiden here

00:15:37.530 --> 00:15:39.960
so he became a priest instead.

00:15:40.360 --> 00:15:42.080
I'm not a boy anymore...

00:15:42.330 --> 00:15:43.970
Wow, sounds like a romance novel!

00:15:43.970 --> 00:15:45.040
Awesome!

00:15:46.830 --> 00:15:49.060
Anyway, do you have enough 
for the offering?

00:15:49.060 --> 00:15:51.530
I think we need some more dried foods.

00:15:51.530 --> 00:15:54.050
And something that's more 
in season for summer.

00:15:54.550 --> 00:15:55.400
Okay.

00:15:55.400 --> 00:15:58.640
U-Uh, is there anything 
I can do to help?

00:15:58.910 --> 00:16:02.850
Oh, I appreciate the offer, 
but don't you have work?

00:16:03.060 --> 00:16:05.810
It's okay. My boss is 
in Tokyo right now.

00:16:08.300 --> 00:16:10.170
Hey, assistant.

00:16:10.170 --> 00:16:12.780
You should take off 
that expensive suit.

00:16:13.160 --> 00:16:14.450
Yes.

00:16:14.780 --> 00:16:16.420
I'll lend you some work clothes.

00:16:16.820 --> 00:16:21.710
Okay, we'll let the men do their 
stuff while we go shopping.

00:16:21.710 --> 00:16:23.210
Yay!

00:16:23.440 --> 00:16:25.820
Is this really going to work out?

00:16:25.820 --> 00:16:27.130
I'm gonna take a nap.

00:16:30.740 --> 00:16:33.630
Mako-chan, is there 
anything else you want?

00:16:33.630 --> 00:16:35.120
I'll buy you anything you want!

00:16:35.120 --> 00:16:36.880
Oh, I need some underwear!

00:16:36.880 --> 00:16:37.760
Underwear?!

00:16:59.640 --> 00:17:00.960
It's finished!

00:17:00.960 --> 00:17:02.010
Good work.

00:17:02.010 --> 00:17:05.690
Satoru-kun was a big help.

00:17:05.690 --> 00:17:07.600
Thanks, Satoru-kun.

00:17:07.600 --> 00:17:08.750
I-It's not a big deal.

00:17:09.140 --> 00:17:11.700
So what do we do for dinner?

00:17:11.700 --> 00:17:14.130
The priests aren't allowed 
to eat meat right now.

00:17:14.130 --> 00:17:15.880
Oh, that doesn't apply to me.

00:17:15.880 --> 00:17:16.760
Quiet.

00:17:17.080 --> 00:17:19.310
Thank you, Yoshizumi-san.

00:17:19.310 --> 00:17:20.390
It was nothing.

00:17:20.620 --> 00:17:23.670
Please stay for dinner.

00:17:23.670 --> 00:17:25.860
Oh, I need to get going.

00:17:25.860 --> 00:17:28.340
I need to bring the car 
back to the house.

00:17:28.340 --> 00:17:30.400
Really? That's too bad.

00:17:30.840 --> 00:17:33.130
Please join us tomorrow, then.

00:17:33.130 --> 00:17:33.900
Yes.

00:17:36.900 --> 00:17:39.220
Is this first time you've 
seen a wreath before?

00:17:39.220 --> 00:17:40.440
Oh, yes.

00:17:40.440 --> 00:17:44.870
I believe that the summer cleansing 
is when you pass through the wreath

00:17:44.870 --> 00:17:47.100
to cleanse impurities 
from the past six months

00:17:47.100 --> 00:17:49.610
and protect yourself 
from summer disease.

00:17:49.610 --> 00:17:50.880
Ah, you're quite knowledgeable.

00:17:51.040 --> 00:17:54.150
Oh, I'm sorry. I did some research.

00:17:54.150 --> 00:17:56.280
I didn't know anything before.

00:17:57.440 --> 00:17:59.050
I wouldn't expect young people to know.

00:17:59.430 --> 00:18:01.570
The people who come here tomorrow 
will be looping around

00:18:01.570 --> 00:18:03.270
both sides in a figure eight.

00:18:03.630 --> 00:18:07.350
Those who participate in 
the June summer cleaning

00:18:07.350 --> 00:18:10.230
have a thousand years 
added to their life.

00:18:11.450 --> 00:18:13.940
They're supposed to say that when 
they pass through the wreath..

00:18:14.250 --> 00:18:15.360
What does that do?

00:18:15.630 --> 00:18:19.130
It means that if you go through 
the cleansing, you'll live to be

00:18:19.130 --> 00:18:20.870
a thousand years old.

00:18:22.210 --> 00:18:23.560
That's a little too much!

00:18:23.560 --> 00:18:25.700
We're not supposed to live 
as long as the gods!

00:18:25.700 --> 00:18:27.620
Well, it's not meant 
to be taken literally.

00:18:28.110 --> 00:18:31.030
Live to be a thousand years

00:18:32.260 --> 00:18:33.390
old...

00:18:43.460 --> 00:18:45.250
Yep, that's right.

00:18:46.200 --> 00:18:48.100
We're asking the gods 
to share their life.

00:18:48.870 --> 00:18:50.520
That might be it.

00:19:05.140 --> 00:19:07.470
Whoa, what are you writing?

00:19:07.470 --> 00:19:09.750
This is the prayer that will be 
used for the cleansing tomorrow.

00:19:10.060 --> 00:19:12.200
You work too hard, man.

00:19:12.200 --> 00:19:13.830
It's the same prayer every year.

00:19:13.830 --> 00:19:15.210
Why not just use a computer?

00:19:16.810 --> 00:19:19.530
That would be easier,

00:19:19.530 --> 00:19:24.390
but a priest's prayer is made 
on behalf of many people.

00:19:24.990 --> 00:19:29.820
I want to write the prayer 
by hand so the gods hear it.

00:19:31.100 --> 00:19:32.880
You lose!

00:19:32.880 --> 00:19:33.990
What?!

00:19:33.990 --> 00:19:36.820
Well, I need to get going.

00:19:37.380 --> 00:19:38.920
Are you staying here tonight?

00:19:38.920 --> 00:19:40.770
We start early tomorrow morning.

00:19:40.770 --> 00:19:43.100
Oh, Satoru-kun's using the room

00:19:43.100 --> 00:19:45.780
you used to use, so you'll 
have to sleep here.

00:19:45.780 --> 00:19:46.830
What?

00:19:47.050 --> 00:19:48.600
I'll sleep with the teenage girls, then!

00:19:48.600 --> 00:19:50.030
Absolutely not!

00:19:51.100 --> 00:19:52.400
I'll see you tomorrow.

00:19:52.400 --> 00:19:54.390
Yep. Thanks, Sis.

00:19:54.820 --> 00:19:57.160
The bath's ready, sir.

00:19:57.410 --> 00:19:59.060
Thank you, Satoru-kun.

00:19:59.060 --> 00:20:01.650
Right, Dad. Go take your bath.

00:20:01.650 --> 00:20:03.140
There's a lot of people waiting.

00:20:03.650 --> 00:20:06.870
So, how about I wash your back for you?

00:20:06.870 --> 00:20:08.720
You're scaring me.

00:20:09.150 --> 00:20:12.310
Your father and Takami-san 
seem pretty close.

00:20:12.310 --> 00:20:15.560
Yep, they've been friends 
since they were kids.

00:20:15.840 --> 00:20:19.660
Oh, when will your father 
perform the Misogi?

00:20:20.110 --> 00:20:21.180
Tomorrow morning?

00:20:21.180 --> 00:20:22.480
Right now.

00:20:22.480 --> 00:20:24.330
He performs Misogi every 
time he takes a bath.

00:20:24.330 --> 00:20:24.950
Huh?

00:20:24.950 --> 00:20:28.740
I thought it only counted if you were 
under a waterfall or in the ocean!

00:20:28.740 --> 00:20:30.450
Of course not.

00:20:30.810 --> 00:20:34.010
Oh, so you can perform 
Misogi in the bath.

00:20:34.010 --> 00:20:36.080
We had a special room 
for it at my shrine.

00:20:36.470 --> 00:20:38.490
Your shrine's bigger than ours.

00:20:41.420 --> 00:20:42.380
Gin!

00:20:43.910 --> 00:20:46.170
Sorry about all the noise today.

00:20:46.170 --> 00:20:49.320
I've gotten used to it. 
Why apologize now?

00:20:49.800 --> 00:20:51.810
Festivals are also important for us.

00:20:52.490 --> 00:20:55.520
So, Gin, I'm sorry about yesterday.

00:20:55.810 --> 00:20:59.730
What's this? Did you already 
solve your problem?

00:21:00.050 --> 00:21:05.180
No... I'll be busy tomorrow, so there's 
no point in worrying about it.

00:21:05.700 --> 00:21:08.950
And panicking won't help 
me find an answer.

00:21:10.170 --> 00:21:12.030
Well, wish us luck tomorrow.

00:21:12.030 --> 00:21:13.690
I'll do that.

00:21:14.090 --> 00:21:19.290
Right, tell Yoshitomo to act more 
like a priest while he's at it.

00:21:20.520 --> 00:21:21.500
I'll let him know.

00:21:24.310 --> 00:21:26.230
What did Gintaro-sama say?

00:21:28.790 --> 00:21:31.520
As usual, he didn't 
seem very interested.

00:21:31.520 --> 00:21:34.550
He said that you need to 
act more like a priest.

00:21:34.550 --> 00:21:36.150
That's no good.

00:21:36.570 --> 00:21:40.050
Oh, right. We have 
another fox spirit now.

00:21:40.050 --> 00:21:41.360
She's called Haru-chan.

00:21:42.900 --> 00:21:44.040
Hey, Uncle Yoshitomo,

00:21:44.860 --> 00:21:47.000
why did you stop being a priest?

00:21:47.000 --> 00:21:49.460
Why did I stop?

00:21:49.460 --> 00:21:50.970
Because it's not really my thing.

00:21:50.970 --> 00:21:52.580
I don't think so.

00:21:56.050 --> 00:21:57.500
I'm getting old.

00:21:58.060 --> 00:21:59.930
You're getting old?

00:21:59.930 --> 00:22:01.790
It's time to go to bed.

00:22:06.580 --> 00:22:11.020
It's been a while since the last time 
I talked to the old Inari-no-Okami.

00:22:11.740 --> 00:22:14.200
I guess I won't be able to sleep tomorrow.

00:22:33.550 --> 00:22:37.610
<i>Tomorrow is June 30th, 
the summer cleansing ceremony.</i>

00:24:10.010 --> 00:24:21.930
<b>Preview</b>

00:24:10.010 --> 00:24:21.930
<b>Silver Fox</b>

00:24:11.370 --> 00:24:15.050
Those who participate in the 
June summer cleaning have

00:24:15.050 --> 00:24:18.040
a thousand years added to their life.

00:24:18.770 --> 00:24:21.640
May fortune always be with you.

00:24:22.040 --> 00:25:25.050
<b>Summer Cleansing</b>

00:24:22.160 --> 00:24:25.050
Next time on the final episode: 
"Summer Cleansing."
